  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Metro Exodus Gold Edition",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/6512/450x258/metro-exodus-gold-edition-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1790600400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/6512-buy-metro-exodus-gold-edition-pc-steam/",
      "user": "Broeselmeister",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/7442856-1657446954.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Great Game, I personally like it very much. I think those semi Open World areas fit the theme of the game a lot. Metro always rewarded it at least a bit if you were to explore the area more than need be to get some extra ammo or money. This Game leans a bit more into that aspect and really rewards you for doin some extra exploring in the open areas."
    },
    {
      "game": "Metro: Last Light Redux",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/188/450x258/metro-last-light-redux-pc-mac-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1790600400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/188-buy-metro-last-light-redux-pc-mac-game-steam/",
      "user": "Broeselmeister",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/7442856-1657446954.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "nice and short game, for the price definetly worth it. I do think its a good improvement from the already solid 2033. This one is a bit more fast paced and more action than horror. So it goes a bit away from one of the more interesting aspects of 2033"
    },
    {
      "game": "The Plucky Squire",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/12124/450x258/the-plucky-squire-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1790600400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/12124-buy-the-plucky-squire-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Filaraki",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/27591431-1788642190.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "The Plucky Squire is a wonderfully creative and charming adventure that feels like a love letter to childhood imagination. Its core mechanic—seamlessly leaping between the 2D pages of a storybook and a fully realized 3D desk environment—is brilliantly executed and delivers some truly inventive puzzles. Combined with gorgeous visuals and a playful variety of arcade-style minigames, the overall experience is overflowing with heart. \n\n\n\nAs echoed across critic reviews on Metacritic, the game is held back from perfection by a lack of challenge and a tendency to hold the player’s hand. Combat remains fairly simple throughout, and an overly talkative script often explains puzzle mechanics before you get the chance to figure them out yourself. \n\n\n\nThe Verdict:\n\n If you are looking for an ultra-tough, high-stakes action game, this might feel a bit too gentle. But if you want a cozy, visually captivating, and inventive puzzle-adventure, The Plucky Squire is well worth a spot in your Steam library."
    },
    {
      "game": "Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles: Shredder's Revenge",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/8441/450x258/teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-shredder-s-revenge-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1790600400",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/8441-buy-teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-shredder-s-revenge-pc-steam/",
      "user": "BranjoHello",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Asked the support if the store plans to sell Ultimate Edition in the future, they replied (quickly) \"don't know, we'll see, keep the game wishlisted\".\n\n\n\nFew days later, I saw the price of this drop quite a lot and I thought \"well, even if it isn't UE, still worth the price\", so I bought it.\n\n\n\nRedeemed on Steam and actually got the UE (probably a Humble Bundle code from last month, which I missed and how got what I wanted waaay cheaper).\n\n\n\nSo happy, love this store! \\o/"
    }
